const body = `<h1>3.3b — Multi-Branch Menu: Building a Game Menu</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Town Menu</h3>
        <p>Most games have menus: Shop, Inn, Blacksmith, Leave Town. Each choice triggers different behavior. An else-if chain is the perfect tool for this.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>TownMenu</code>. Hardcode an <code>int choice</code> (try 1 through 5, one at a time).</p>
        <ol>
            <li>choice == 1 → Print "You enter the shop. A merchant greets you."</li>
            <li>choice == 2 → Print "You rest at the inn. HP restored!"</li>
            <li>choice == 3 → Print "The blacksmith sharpens your sword. +2 attack."</li>
            <li>choice == 4 → Print "You leave town. Safe travels!"</li>
            <li>Anything else → Print "Invalid choice. Try again."</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Trace Challenge</h3>
        <p>Swap two of the conditions — move choice 4 above choice 1. Run with choice=4. Does anything change? What if choice=1? When does order NOT matter in an else-if chain?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Booleans &amp; if Statements</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/scanner.html">Scanner Input</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
